<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meles Zenawi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–<a href="/years/2012">2012</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meles Zenawi was leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigray-peoples-liberation-front">Tigray People's Liberation Front</a> and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-peoples-revolutionary-democratic-front">EPRDF</a> coalition that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a> in 1991. He was president of the Transitional Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and, from 1995, prime minister of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia until his death in 2012. His government introduced ethnic federalism and pursued state-led growth while suppressing opposition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meles-zenawi.jpg" alt="Meles Zenawi" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: World Economic Forum · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meles_Zenawi_-_World_Economic_Forum_Annual_Meeting_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
